WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.200
(classical music)

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.630
- [Narrator] One of the newest additions

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.470
to the skyline in Hamburg, Germany

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:08.815
is a concert hall fit for a modern Mozart.

00:00:08.815 --> 00:00:11.648
(classical music)

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.150
The Elbphilharmonie is
considered one of the largest

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.800
and most acoustically advanced
concert venues in the world.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.570
Made up of three concert halls,

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.050
the Elbphilharmonie seats
more than 2,800 visitors.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.220
The Great Concert Hall, the
largest of the three halls,

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.410
has 10,000 unique acoustic
panels that were designed

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.780
using computer algorithms to
create the best possible sound.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.180
Each panel contains one million cells

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.950
that shape the sound by
either absorbing the waves

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:45.000
or having them reverberate
through the space.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.120
The curved design of the cells can be seen

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.250
replicated throughout the entire building.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.000
Not to be outdone, the glass exterior

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.030
of The Elbphilharmonie built
atop a former warehouse

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.200
is just as spectacular as the interior.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.300
The structure rises above the Elbe River

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.510
and mirrors the water's wave and shine.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.530
To mark the opening night,

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.410
the exterior featured a light show

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:12.110
timed to the music being
played within The Great Hall.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.150
With multiple events almost every day,

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.970
The Elbphilharmonie is
a must see for music

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:20.270
and math lovers a like.

